    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the inboard flap track and carriage assembly, listing the roller, the bearing hardware and the track itself with the pairing note that governs which roller may run on which track.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the inboard flap track, the carriage and the roller and bearing assembly, together with the pivot hardware and the bearing cover, for one wing.",
      "figure_note": "The carriage is shown at the fully retracted position; the roller envelope at full extension is shown dashed because it determines the clearance to the flap position sensing bracket. Item 30 is the roller and its profile must match the track surface treatment given at item 10: a crowned roller runs only on a nitrided track. The obsolete clamp at item 60 is shown for identification on aircraft that still carry it and is not refitted at any removal."
    },
